somy of the short arm of chromosome 19\t\tpartial duplication of chromosome 19p|partial duplication of the short arm of chromosome type 19|partial trisomy of chromosome 19p|partial trisomy of the short arm of chromosome 19\thttp://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018659\t\t\tOrphanet:447985|UMLS:C4518508|http://identifiers.org/medgen/1380854\tdisease_grouping|ordo_group_of_disorders\n13038: MONDO:0018660\tbiolink:Disease\themophilia\tHemophilia is a genetic disorder characterized by spontaneous hemorrhage or prolonged bleeding due to factor VIII or IX deficiency.\tDOID:0061030|GARD:0010418|MEDGEN:146334|MedDRA:10061992|NCIT:C3093|Orphanet:448|SCTID:90935002|UMLS:C0684275\tmondo-rare.json\themophilia\t\themophilia\thttp://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018660\t\t\tDOID:0061030|NCIT:C3093|Orphanet:448|UMLS:C0684275|http://identifiers.org/medgen/146334|http://identifiers.org/snomedct/90935002\tdisease_grouping|doid_rare|gard_rare|nord_rare|ordo_group_of_disorders|otar|rare\n13039: MONDO:0018661\tbiolink:Disease\tZika virus infectious disease\tMosquito-born virus disease characterized by a clinical course that may be asymptomatic or mild with fever, conjunctivitis, muscle and joint pain, headache, exanthema, but may also be associated with severe neurological (meningitis, meningoencephalitis and myelitis) and auto-immune (Guillain-Barre syndrome) complications, as well as a potential increase of birth defects (microcephaly) if the infection occurs during pregnancy.\tDOID:0060478|GARD:0012894|ICD10CM:A92.5|MEDGEN:547236|MESH:D000071243|NCIT:C128423|Orphanet:448237|SCTID:3928002|UMLS:C0276289|icd11.foundation:1401438580\tmondo-rare.json\tZikV infection|Zika|Zika fever|Zika virus caused disease or disorder|Zika virus disease|Zika virus disease or disorder|Zika virus infection|Zika virus infectious disease|congenital Zika syndrome|congenital Zika virus infection|fever, Zika\t\tZikV infection|Zika|Zika virus caused disease or disorder|Zika virus disease|Zika virus disease or d