64\tbiolink:Disease\tectopia cordis\tA rare congenital anomaly where the heart is formed outside of the thoracic cavity. It is associated with intracardiac lesions and other structural malformations.\tGARD:0021877|HP:0001683|ICD9:746.87|MEDGEN:41703|MESH:D054083|NCIT:C111643|Orphanet:448270|SCTID:78250005|UMLS:C0013580|icd11.foundation:285576893\tmondo-rare.json\tectopia cordis|ectopia cordis (disease)\t\tectopia cordis|ectopia cordis (disease)\thttp://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018664\t\t\tNCIT:C111643|Orphanet:448270|UMLS:C0013580|http://id.who.int/icd/entity/285576893|http://identifiers.org/medgen/41703|http://identifiers.org/mesh/D054083|http://identifiers.org/snomedct/78250005\tgard_rare|nord_rare|ordo_disorder|ordo_morphological_anomaly|orphanet_rare|rare\n13043: MONDO:0018666\tbiolink:Disease\thepatoblastoma\tHepatoblastoma (HB) is a malignant hepatic tumor and is the most common pediatric liver cancer. It is characterized by anorexia, weight loss and an enlarged abdomen. HB is more common in patients with familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP), and can occur in patients with other pre-existing liver conditions. About 5% of HB cases are associated with genetic factors, especially overgrowth syndromes, such as Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome (BWS) or hemihypertrophy.\tDOID:687|EFO:1000292|GARD:0002657|ICD10CM:C22.2|ICDO:8970/3|MEDGEN:61644|MESH:D018197|MedDRA:10062001|NANDO:2200046|NCIT:C3728|ONCOTREE:LIHB|Orphanet:449|UMLS:C0206624|icd11.foundation:1241693063|icd11.foundation:1556608523\tmondo-rare.json\tHBL|hepatoblastoma|hepatoblastoma, malignant|paediatric embryonal hepatoma|paediatric hepatoblastoma|pediatric embryonal hepatoma|pediatric hepatoblastoma\t\tHBL|hepatoblastoma|hepatoblastoma, malignant|paediatric embryonal hepatoma|paediatric hepatoblastoma|pediatric embryonal hepatoma|pediatric hepatoblastoma\thttp://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018666\t\t\tDOID:687|NCIT:C3728|Orphanet:449|UMLS:C0206624|http://id.who.int/icd/entity/1241693063|http://id.who.