 venom causing toxic effect|snake venom poisoning|toxic effect of bite of venomous snake\tOrphanet:449285|http://identifiers.org/snomedct/61288004\tgard_rare|nord_rare|ordo_clinical_situation|ordo_disorder|orphanet_rare|rare\n13047: MONDO:0018670\tbiolink:Disease\tsymptomatic form of fragile X syndrome in female carrier\t\tGARD:0017783|MEDGEN:1814467|Orphanet:449291|UMLS:C5681104\tmondo-rare.json\t\t\t\thttp://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018670\t\t\tUMLS:C5681104|http://identifiers.org/medgen/1814467\tgard_rare|nord_rare|rare\n13048: MONDO:0018671\tbiolink:Disease\tIgG4-related kidney disease\t\tGARD:0021882|MEDGEN:1708840|NANDO:1200930|Orphanet:449395|UMLS:C5392056|icd11.foundation:1877692678\tmondo-rare.json\t\t\t\thttp://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018671\t\t\tOrphanet:449395|UMLS:C5392056|http://id.who.int/icd/entity/1877692678|http://identifiers.org/medgen/1708840\tgard_rare|nord_rare|ordo_subtype_of_a_disorder|rare\n13049: MONDO:0018672\tbiolink:Disease\tIgG4-related aortitis\t\tGARD:0021883|MEDGEN:1800431|Orphanet:449400|UMLS:C5569008|icd11.foundation:593151236\tmondo-rare.json\tIgG4-related periaortitis\t\tIgG4-related periaortitis\thttp://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018672\t\t\tOrphanet:449400|UMLS:C5569008|http://id.who.int/icd/entity/593151236|http://identifiers.org/medgen/1800431\tgard_rare|nord_rare|ordo_subtype_of_a_disorder|rare\n13050: MONDO:0018673\tbiolink:Disease\tIgG4-related pachymeningitis\tIdiopathic hypertrophic pachymeningitis (IHP) is a rare disorder causing inflammation and thickening of the outer layer (dura) of the brain and/or spinal cord. IHP can be widespread or cause tumor-like lesions. Before IHP can be diagnosed, other conditions including sarcoidosis, tumors, meningioma, infections (syphilis, tuberculosis, and Lyme disease), and autoimmune diseases (rheumatoid arthritis, Sjogrenbs syndrome, Wegenerbs granulomatosis, and IgG4-related disease) must be ruled out. IHP often presents with headache and cranial nerve impairment. Treatment may involve prednisone and/or an immune suppressing drug. This treatment often improves symptoms, however complete recovery is rare. Surgery may be recommended for people with advanced or severe IHP. Some people with IHP have no symptoms and may not need treatment.\tGARD:0013256|MEDGEN:1627405|Orphanet:449427|SCTID:762282007|UMLS:C4545992|icd11.foundation:1140264879\tmondo-rare.json\tidiopathic hypertrophic cranial pachymeningitis|idiopathic hypertrophic craniospinal pachymeningitis|idiopathic hypertrophic pachymeningitis|idiopathic hypertrophic spinal pachymeningitis\t\tidiopathic hypertrophic pachymeningitis\thttp://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018673\t\tidiopathic hypertrophic cranial pachymeningitis|idiopathic hypertrophic craniospinal pachymeningitis|idiopathic hypertrophic spinal pachymeningitis\tOrphanet:449427|UMLS:C4545992|http://id.who.int/icd/entity/1140264879|http://identifiers.org/medgen/1627405|http://identifiers.org/snomedct/762282007\tgard_rare|nord_rare|ordo_subtype_of_a_disorder|rare\n13051: MONDO:0018674\tbiolink:Disease\tIgG4-related submandibular gland disease\tA chronic fibrotic inflammatory process affecting the salivary gland. Signs and symptoms include firm and painful swelling of the salivary gland, often associated with the presence of salivary gland stones.\tGARD:0021884|MEDGEN:1830092|NCIT:C82887|Orphanet:449432|SCTID:448131008|UMLS:C5679995|icd11.foundation:588811750\tmondo-rare.json\tIgG4-related sialadenitis|Kuttner tumor|Kuttner tumour|Kuttner's tumor|Kuttner's tumour|Küttner tumor|Küttner tumour|chronic sclerosing sialadenitis\t\tIgG4-related sialadenitis|Kuttner tumor|Kuttner tumour|Kuttner's tumor|Kuttner's tumour|Küttner tumor|Küttner tumour|chronic sclerosing sialadenitis\thttp://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018674\t\t\tNCIT:C82887|Orphanet:449432|UMLS:C5679995|http://id.who.int/icd/entity/588811750|http://identifiers.org/medgen/1830092|http://identifiers.org/snomedct/448131008\tgard_rare|nord_rare|ordo_subtype_of_a_disorder|rare\n13052: MONDO:0018675\tbiolink:Disease\tIgG4-related ophthalmic disorder\tA IgG4-related disease that involves the eye.\tGARD:0021885|MEDGEN:1800432|Orphanet:449563|UMLS:C5569009\tmondo-rare.json\tIgG4-related disease of eye|eye IgG4-related disease\t\tIgG4-related disease of eye|eye IgG4-related disease\thttp://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018675\t\t\tOrphanet:449563|UMLS:C5569009|http://identifiers.org/medgen/1800432\tgard_rare|nord_rare|ordo_subtype_of_a_disorder|otar|rare\n13053: MONDO:0018676\tbiolink:Disease\teosinophilic angiocentric fibrosis\t\tGARD:0021886|MEDGEN:1814179|Orphanet:449566|UMLS:C5578050|icd11.foundation:57609544\tmondo-rare.json\tEAF|IgG4-related eosinophilic angiocentric fibrosis|Sinonasal eosinophilic angiocentric fibrosis|eosinophilic angiocentric fibrosis\t\tIgG4-related eosinophilic angiocentric fibrosis|eosinophilic angiocentric fibrosis\thttp://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0018676\t\tEAF|Sinonasal eosinophilic angiocentric fibrosis\tOrphanet:449566|UMLS:C5578050|http://id.who.int/icd/entity/57609544|http://identifiers.org/medgen/1814179\tgard_rare|nord_rare|ordo_disorder|orphanet_rare|rare\n13054: MONDO:0018677\tbiolink:Disease\tvisceral heterotaxy\tA rare, genetic disorder in which symptoms are generally secondary to the abnormal location of the organs within the thoracic, abdominal, or peritoneal cavities. Anatomic and functional problems can include cardiac defects, intestinal malrotation leading to volvulus, biliary atresia, and various defects of the central nervous system, urinary tract, and skeleton.\tDOID:0050545|GARD:0010875|MEDGEN:465273|MedDRA:10059119|MedDRA:10067265|NCIT:C117273|OMIMPS:306955|Orphanet:157769|Orphanet:450|SCTID:14821001|UMLS:C3178805|icd11.foundation:780273165\tmondo-rare.json\theterotaxia|heterotaxia syndrome|heterotaxy syndrome|heterotaxy, visceral|incomplete situs inversus|lateralization defect|partial situs inversus|situs ambiguous|situs ambiguus|visceral heterotaxy\t\theterotaxia|het